WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.327
Molecular modeling in quantum mechanics demands
models that respect physical laws,

00:00:05.407 --> 00:00:10.933
namely invariance and equivariance to rotation and
translation of atomic coordinates.

00:00:11.013 --> 00:00:13.109
This paper introduces GeoMFormer,

00:00:13.189 --> 00:00:19.439
a general and flexible Transformer-based
architecture that learns both invariant and equivariant

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:21.681
molecular representations at once.

00:00:21.761 --> 00:00:26.825
It uses two parallel Transformer streams, one for
each type of representation,

00:00:26.905 --> 00:00:33.551
and bridges them with carefully designed
cross-attention modules so information flows between the two.

00:00:33.631 --> 00:00:38.497
Many prior geometric models turn out to be special
cases of this framework,

00:00:38.577 --> 00:00:44.300
and GeoMFormer sets new state-of-the-art results
across a wide range of molecular tasks.
